  "evidenceNotes": [
    "Every route passes `preset` AND its own `sections`/`quote` (caseStudyContentData.js), so the SHORT/LONG presets in the component are never rendered on a real page; they were still counted for budgets. `preset` itself is not modelled (it only picks default copy).",
    "Route copy is generated by prose()/phrase(); the sample was evaluated with node. The customer-6 first title is \"...before\\n\\u200d\\n\" (a zero-width-joiner line), copied verbatim.",
    "The page always passes tocFromHeadings, so sub-headings appear in the TOC on every real route.",
    "On every case-study-content route the page renders layout2-hero, cs-content-stats, cs-content-article, cs-content-related in that order (CaseStudyContent.jsx); separate components, so no mustImmediatelyFollow."
  ],
